Package: miadi-tide
Version: @VERSION@
Section: misc
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Depends: python (>= 3.11), tmux, coreutils
Maintainer: Miadi <mia@jgwill.com>
Homepage: https://github.com/jgwill/miadi-orchestration-kit
Description: The tide runtime on a Termux phone, its daemon kept in tmux
 The Termux build of miadi-tide: tide from its own venv, built at install
 from the pinned PyPI releases, and miadi-tide-service. Termux has no
 systemd, so the Ubuntu build's tide-runtime.service and
 tide-store-prune.timer become two tmux sessions: tide-runtime runs
 `tide daemon`, and tide-runtime-watchdog starts it again when it stops and
 prunes its snapshot store once a day. Termux:Boot starts both through
 share/miadi/termux-boot/50-miadi-tide.sh. Run `miadi-tide-service ensure`
 once after the first install. The review loop (tan) is not in this build.
